    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0111" n="9" xml:id="pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5686: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-05T10:00:00+08:00">January 5, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 5—2:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Following from American Consul General at Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 4, 11 a.m.</p>
                        <list>
                            <label>1.</label>
                            <item>Entire east line Chinese Eastern Railway now occupied by Japanese
                                troops which practically without meeting opposition reached Suifenho
                                January 3d.</item>
                            <label>2.</label>
                            <item>Morishima, Japanese Consul General, informed me that he reached
                                agreement December 29th with local Soviet Consul General to the
                                effect that Soviet Government would not object to Japanese troops
                                going as far as Suifenho. Soviet Consulate General confirms
                                this.”</item>
                        </list>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
